# REVIEW_INFRASTRUCTURE_FIX — narrowest possible scope.
#
# The bash review runner must check out with LF on every platform. Without this,
# a clone using the Git for Windows default core.autocrlf=true writes CRLF into
# the script and bash refuses to execute it:
#   RUN_CODEX_REVIEW.sh: line 13: $'\r': command not found
#   RUN_CODEX_REVIEW.sh: line 14: set: pipefail: invalid option name
#   exit 2
# That breaks the review under Git Bash and WSL. Found by executing the runner
# in an autocrlf=true clone, not by inspection.
#
# Deliberately NOT normalising anything else:
#   - no `* text=auto`, no `*.ts`/`*.json` rules. Product source is frozen; its
#     checkout semantics are not this fix's business, and the v2 canonical hash
#     is line-ending independent anyway, so nothing needs them.
#   - no rule for *.ps1. PowerShell reads either ending, and a repo-wide *.ps1
#     rule would also reach install/install.ps1, which is outside review scope.
#   - no rule for *.mjs. Node executes CRLF scripts correctly (verified).
reports/codex-package/RUN_CODEX_REVIEW.sh text eol=lf
